+- **Main Interface (Map View)**: **Reordered buttons** (end turn, city change arrows) and wrapped them in a **pretty panel**. Added buttons to unit stack, selected unit. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5726+) Added **help text box** (`DefaultHelpArea`) (on the left side) optional **width adjustment** (negative value shrinks it). Make **x and y positions** (resolution-scaled), and **width** (hard pixel; not resolution-scaled) of the **unit bar** (`PlotListPanel`) **adjustable**, and **fix horizontal overflow of unit bar into scoreboard** when unit bar is full and scoreboard is hovered on (or toggle lock scoreboard hover is ON) (see [KI#124](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#124---fixed-likely-base-advciv-issue-map-view-unit-bar-overflows-into-hoveredexpanded-scoreboard)). (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5503+) Make **left-click on GP bar** open the **corresponding city's city screen**. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5723+) Added a **Toggle show annotations** (Alt + S **captions**, Alt + X **BFC marks**) button (next to the other buttons **above the Minimap**); the toggled state **persists on save and load**; reorganized buttons as part of this change (this takes the Event Log's former HUD icon former (it gets another one instead)). See [README.md (Map annotations)](/README.md#map-annotations).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5533+) **Scoreboard**: do **not draw beyond** bottom of commerce sliders (previously it would overflow beyond top of the screen), add **+ (up) and - (down) scroll buttons** to choose **first and last leader shown** when the **number of leaders is high** (e.g., if there are 48 leaders to display and the scoreboard can only show ~30 leaders max). Note: the Info screen's score tab allows to see all leaders so this is a fine trade-off to avoid vertical overflow. Add a **Lock scoreboard hover toggle button** so scoreboard is always hovered on even without hover (e.g., to see power ratios without having to hover). Note: in first turns of the game this effectively has no effect since power ratios are not yet visible. Change in [Scoreboard.py](/Assets/Python/BUG/Scoreboard.py) and [CvMainInterface.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMainInterface.py). See [README.md (Scoreboard)](/README.md#scoreboard).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5507+) **Main Interface (civilization flag):** **Removed the civilization flag** from the production buttons bar (next to minimap) to show more buttons instead and have a more efficient display. Instead, added **optional compact top-left civilization flag** (with same preserved BtS hover/click behavior) (if **enabled**, left **top text spacing is shifted to make room for the compact flag**). Unlike base AdvCiv, this **optional flag** is **also visible in city screen** because it does not interfere with bottom city-action buttons. This flag is useful to know player civ, hover for player traits, and click to capital's city screen. Default disabled (tunable) as it can be distracting and undesired.
 - **Worker recommendation highlights disabled**: turned off tile coloring for "worker-recommended plot to improve" (in `CvGame::updateColoredPlots` within `CvGameInterface.cpp`). Reasons: (1) avoids extra computation in both debug ([see for related info this autoplay info](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/Modding_Ressources/README.md#how-to-autoplay-let-the-ai-play-for-you-super-fast-gameplay--testing-tool-in-map-loaded-save-file-new-game-etc-view)) and normal play; (2) our worker logic now relies on `CvUnitAI::AI_bestCityBuild`, so the vanilla highlight often disagrees and can mislead; (3) the highlight was easily confused with **city site** recommendations. City-site suggestions remain enabled and intentionally prominent; in practice, they frequently pick **strong** locations—quite often as good as, or better than, typical manual choices. See [Settlers (AI)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md#settlers-ai). *Note:* the **displayed recommended settle city plots** don’t always match what the AI would settle if it were playing your civ in autoplay; the UI hint path may be (not sure) using a different logic from the reworked/optimized `AIFoundValue::evaluate`. Treat them as general information, not guarantees.

